  "instruction": "The overnight alert on Marijke Arendse looks like a genuine credential compromise and GRC has a regulator evidence session on Thursday morning. Before Solène briefs them I need the honest picture: how many credential objects the identity and its linked payments principal actually need contained at the current inventory snapshot, how many of what the register shows we can genuinely revoke ourselves once the rotated and owner-held grants are set aside, whether Halyard's invalidation job changes the date, and what a tenant-wide sign-out would really involve. Book the owner review window that works and leave Solène a draft she can take into the session. Anything that needs Beatriz or Nienke should be flagged, not assumed.",
